SUMMARY:Abendmusik: from Buxtehude to Bach
DESCRIPTION:Experience Buxtehude’s profound influence on Bach \nIn 1705\, the 20-year-old Johann Sebastian Bach journeyed 400 kilometres on foot from Arnstadt to Lübeck to meet and learn from the great composer Dietrich Buxtehude\, then aged 70. During Bach’s three-month stay he would have experienced Buxtehude’s legendary Abendmusiken\, or “Evening Concerts”\, with their mix of sacred vocal and instrumental music presented in St. Mary’s Church. \nOur own special Abendmusik invites you to experience Buxtehude’s profound influence on Bach\, and meet other musical travellers along the way: Johann Christoph Bach\, Graupner\, Doles\, Reincken and Krebs. \nCome\, refresh your spirit and soul with our Abendmusik offering\, featuring the Tafelmusik Chamber Choir and members of the Tafelmusik Baroque Orchestra. Buy your tickets for Abendmusik: from Buxtehude to Bach on May 15\, 2026 at tafelmusik.org
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/abendmusik-from-buxtehude-to-bach/
LOCATION:427 Bloor Street West\, 427 Bloor St W\, Toronto\, ON M5S 1X6\, Canada\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 1X6
CATEGORIES:Live Music,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/abendmusik-from-buxtehude-to-bach.png
END:VEVENT
