SUMMARY:Tribal Crackling Wind presents Worn Inheritance
DESCRIPTION:Award-winning choreographer Peter Chin returns to Toronto with Worn Inheritance\, a contemporary dance program presented by Tribal Crackling Wind\, running May 15–17\, 2026 at the Winchester Street Theatre. \nThe performance features solo works by Chin\, performed by William Lau\, Marina Acevedo\, and Derek Souvannavong\, exploring themes of identity\, memory\, and cultural heritage. Drawing from diverse influences across multiple countries\, each piece uses elements like traditional performance styles and symbolic cloth to reflect personal and ancestral stories. \nTickets prices range from $25 to $35. 
URL:https://nowtoronto.com/event/tribal-crackling-wind-presents-worn-inheritance/
LOCATION:Winchester Street Theatre\, 80 Winchester St\, Old Toronto\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M4X 1B2
CATEGORIES:Dance
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://nowtoronto.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/tribal-crackling-wind-presents-worn-inheritance.png
END:VEVENT
